# RNUI — AI agent rules

RNUI is a **React Native design system and UI kit**. When editing this repo or generating screens that use RNUI:

## Must do

- Read `.ai/rnui.manifest.json` first for AI metadata paths.
- Prefer **existing RNUI components** from `.ai/component-registry.json` before creating custom UI.
- Use **theme/tokens** from `@truongdq01/headless` — never random hex colors or magic spacing numbers.
- Wrap the app with **`ThemeProvider`** once at root (`withGestureRoot={false}` if app already has `GestureHandlerRootView`).
- Import UI from **`@truongdq01/ui`**:

```tsx
import { ThemeProvider, Button, Card, Input, Stack, Typography } from '@truongdq01/ui';
```

- Keep screens **mobile-first**, **accessible** (`accessibilityLabel` on icon-only actions), **TypeScript-safe**.
- Follow `.ai/design-rules.md` and `.ai/screen-generation.md`.

## Must not do

- Add new dependencies unless truly necessary.
- Duplicate Button, Card, Input, Typography, Stack, or other exported components.
- Modify package public APIs without explicit user request.
- Put styled UI in `tokens` or business logic in `ui` — respect package boundaries (see `.ai/package-map.json`).
- Use `any`, `@ts-ignore`, or eslint-disable.

## Package boundaries

| Package | Role |
| ------- | ---- |
| `@truongdq01/tokens` | Design tokens only |
| `@truongdq01/headless` | Theme, hooks, a11y, logic |
| `@truongdq01/ui` | Styled components |
| `@truongdq01/themes` | Brand presets |

## Validation

Run `bun run ai:check` after adding AI metadata. Run `bun run typecheck` and `bun run lint` after code changes.

Full guide: [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md)
